But there are three practical approaches, in order of elegance:

### 1. MCP Server (best — already in your v2 Phase 1 plan)
Instead of detecting files *after*, Claude pushes decisions *as they happen*. Your user adds Continuum as an MCP server in their Claude config:

```json
// ~/.claude/settings.json
"mcpServers": {
  "continuum": {
    "url": "https://your-railway-url/mcp"
  }
}
```

Now Claude can call `record_decision` and `search_context` during conversations. No file watching, no uploads

